00:00:00,010 --> 00:0o:04,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:05,652 --> 00:00:07,403
Hold on a moment.

2
00:00:07,487 --> 00:00:10,448
What's this Landmark Hotel
you're talking about?

3
00:00:10,532 --> 00:00:13,034
Does the Expo plan include accommodations?

4
00:00:13,117 --> 00:00:16,955
Well, you see,
this isn't just about the Expo.

5
00:00:17,038 --> 00:00:18,039
What?

6
00:00:19,582 --> 00:00:21,584
You see, this proposed Expo site…

7
00:00:22,377 --> 00:00:26,339
We're going to expand it a bit
and make it into an IR zone.

8
00:00:26,422 --> 00:00:28,716
-IR?
-Yes.

9
00:00:29,384 --> 00:00:31,970
It has a hotel, a casino,
commercial facilities,

10
00:00:32,053 --> 00:00:34,305
and an international convention center.

11
00:00:34,389 --> 00:00:38,768
Combined,
they create an "Integrated Resort."

12
00:00:38,852 --> 00:00:42,897
I want to build Asia's largest resort
right here in Konan City.

13
00:00:42,981 --> 00:00:45,984
Something like Las Vegas
or Marina Bay Sands?

14
00:00:46,067 --> 00:00:49,404
What we're aiming for
is one step beyond that.

15
00:00:50,321 --> 00:00:54,159
We'll boldly deregulate and implement
a special tax system.

16
00:00:54,659 --> 00:00:55,785
I want to make this

17
00:00:56,411 --> 00:01:00,415
a place where international companies,
talent, and capital gather.

18
00:01:00,498 --> 00:01:02,876
A special city-state, so to speak.

19
00:01:03,543 --> 00:01:05,670
You mean a special economic zone?

20
00:01:05,753 --> 00:01:06,754
Yeah.

21
00:01:06,838 --> 00:01:09,757
If so, wouldn't that require
legal adjustments?

22
00:01:09,841 --> 00:01:13,928
That won't be a problem.
I'll pass whatever bills are necessary.

23
00:01:15,638 --> 00:01:16,848
Mr. Kuze.

24
00:01:17,557 --> 00:01:19,142
Do you see?

25
00:01:20,059 --> 00:01:22,520
This is the next national-scale project.

26
00:01:23,188 --> 00:01:27,442
You certainly understand Japan's current
position in the world, don't you?

27
00:01:27,525 --> 00:01:30,320
To remain a developed nation,

28
00:01:31,029 --> 00:01:33,406
don't you think this is our last chance?

29
00:01:34,365 --> 00:01:38,286
But will the mayor show any interest?

30
00:01:38,369 --> 00:01:41,623
I would like you to talk
to the mayor about this, Mr. Kuze.

31
00:01:42,582 --> 00:01:47,879
This plan requires the cooperation
of the local people.

32
00:01:48,963 --> 00:01:49,797
But…

33
00:01:49,881 --> 00:01:54,802
The next election is coming up,
can't we help each other out?

34
00:01:56,137 --> 00:01:58,181
SUPER TECH EXPO KEY PERSON
REPRESENTATIVE FURUSE

35
00:02:00,141 --> 00:02:03,102
WILL JAPAN ESCAPE THIS ECONOMIC SLUMP
AND RECLAIM ITS PLACE IN THE WORLD?

36
00:02:13,238 --> 00:02:16,491
Oh! Isn't this Shion Hoshimiya's
Spiritual Floor Plan?

37
00:02:16,574 --> 00:02:17,617
You know it?

38
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:22,455
They take a house in town and do
a reading on its floor plan.

39
00:02:22,538 --> 00:02:26,834
"Because this land used to be a graveyard,
it has a strong spiritual presence.

40
00:02:26,918 --> 00:02:30,964
The open-air corridor facing the courtyard
becomes a perfect pathway for spirits."

41
00:02:31,047 --> 00:02:31,965
Ridiculous.

42
00:02:32,048 --> 00:02:34,008
No one believes that stuff nowadays.

43
00:02:34,092 --> 00:02:37,720
No, floor plans are super important.
They change the whole vibe.

44
00:02:37,804 --> 00:02:39,264
Stop spitting!

45
00:02:39,347 --> 00:02:42,308
Some people really care about feng shui
and home divinations.

46
00:02:42,392 --> 00:02:45,436
Even some of our clients
are super obsessed with it.

47
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:47,647
They overdo it,
and mess up the circulation plan.

48
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:49,107
Defeats the whole purpose.

49
00:02:49,857 --> 00:02:53,361
This fortune teller is the cult leader
of Yoshin no Michi, right?

50
00:02:53,444 --> 00:02:55,822
That new religious movement?

51
00:02:56,864 --> 00:02:58,700
Wow, she looks shady!

52
00:02:59,283 --> 00:03:00,702
Wow, how flashy.

53
00:03:00,785 --> 00:03:03,204
Is she plotting some kind
of spiritual scam?

54
00:03:03,287 --> 00:03:05,832
Like telling people to buy a vase
to fix their fortune?

55
00:03:05,915 --> 00:03:07,959
That won't work in this day and age.

56
00:03:08,042 --> 00:03:11,838
It says lining up water buckets
improves luck. Should we try?

57
00:03:11,921 --> 00:03:13,131
Let's do it.

58
00:03:42,076 --> 00:03:43,661
Huh?

59
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:50,376
Why?

60
00:03:53,796 --> 00:03:56,257
No!

61
00:04:16,277 --> 00:04:17,945
There was a bit of an incident.

62
00:04:20,948 --> 00:04:24,160
"The landlady suddenly went hysterical
in the front yard."

63
00:04:24,243 --> 00:04:26,120
A house haunted by demons?

64
00:04:26,204 --> 00:04:29,624
Isn't this the house
from that magazine's latest issue?

65
00:04:30,541 --> 00:04:32,085
Oh, you're right.

66
00:04:32,168 --> 00:04:35,421
She pointed out that this house
has an ominous layout,

67
00:04:35,505 --> 00:04:37,507
and then the landlady went hysterical?

68
00:04:37,590 --> 00:04:39,509
Floor plans really do matter.

69
00:04:39,592 --> 00:04:43,179
Calling it "demon-haunted"
is a bit dramatic though.

70
00:04:44,305 --> 00:04:47,016
Are you sure she was just being dramatic?

71
00:04:49,727 --> 00:04:53,398
At Hampton Court Palace in England,

72
00:04:54,107 --> 00:04:57,360
a ghost was captured on security cameras.

73
00:04:59,153 --> 00:05:01,489
At the Tower of London,

74
00:05:02,156 --> 00:05:07,703
the wandering spirit of Anne Boleyn
has been spotted numerous times.

75
00:05:09,622 --> 00:05:14,836
Historic buildings are always
associated with mysterious phenomena.

76
00:05:15,670 --> 00:05:16,587
What?

77
00:05:16,671 --> 00:05:18,381
Are you the type to believe that?

78
00:05:18,464 --> 00:05:21,384
Well, he is kind of like a demon himself.

79
00:05:23,511 --> 00:05:28,099
First, I would like to hear
what the landlady has to say though.

80
00:05:28,182 --> 00:05:31,769
The one in charge should be here soon.

81
00:05:31,853 --> 00:05:33,146
What?

82
00:05:34,439 --> 00:05:35,773
Good morning.

83
00:05:36,941 --> 00:05:40,194
You're all here.
Are you up to no good again?

84
00:05:40,278 --> 00:05:41,612
Let me introduce her.

85
00:05:41,696 --> 00:05:45,575
She is our savior,
the lawyer, Naokiman. Applause.

86
00:05:47,285 --> 00:05:48,870
My name is Aso!

87
00:05:49,954 --> 00:05:51,122
Welcome!

88
00:05:52,039 --> 00:05:54,083
No way. Why do I have to do it?

89
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:56,419
I'm currently suspended.

90
00:05:56,502 --> 00:06:00,131
I'm not your errand girl, Mr. Uramawashi.

91
00:06:00,631 --> 00:06:05,178
Saving people who are suffering
is your motto, isn't it?

92
00:06:05,261 --> 00:06:08,139
Please don't just bring up
my motto like that.

93
00:06:08,222 --> 00:06:09,974
I choose my own work.

94
00:06:11,184 --> 00:06:13,728
I see, so that's how it is.

95
00:06:13,811 --> 00:06:16,022
-Huh?
-This job is too much for you.

96
00:06:16,105 --> 00:06:18,524
-Too much?
-I see.

97
00:06:18,608 --> 00:06:20,943
There's no way you can do it.

98
00:06:21,027 --> 00:06:22,945
I can't do it? What the heck?

99
00:06:26,199 --> 00:06:27,575
You must be scared.

100
00:06:27,658 --> 00:06:29,076
Excuse me?

101
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:32,371
What are you saying? I'm not scared!

102
00:06:32,455 --> 00:06:33,456
Then, take it on.

103
00:06:33,539 --> 00:06:34,624
No way.

104
00:06:35,625 --> 00:06:37,793
Hey, are you listening to me?

105
00:06:37,877 --> 00:06:40,922
I'm not going, you know.
I am definitely not going.

106
00:06:41,464 --> 00:06:44,258
Mr. Uramawashi! Hey, Mr. Uramawashi!

107
00:06:44,342 --> 00:06:47,720
Jeez, why do I have to…

108
00:06:48,554 --> 00:06:51,182
OUKA

109
00:07:01,692 --> 00:07:04,153
Hello.

110
00:07:10,493 --> 00:07:12,370
Excuse me.

111
00:07:13,704 --> 00:07:15,748
Is anyone here?

112
00:07:22,338 --> 00:07:23,381
Hey!

113
00:07:24,882 --> 00:07:26,717
What are you doing?

114
00:07:26,801 --> 00:07:29,804
I have business with the landlord,
Ms. Ouka.

115
00:07:29,887 --> 00:07:32,056
I'm not a thief or something!

116
00:07:32,139 --> 00:07:34,141
Ms. Ouka isn't here.

117
00:07:35,184 --> 00:07:36,185
What?

118
00:07:44,944 --> 00:07:45,903
Sorry.

119
00:07:48,739 --> 00:07:50,908
Hey, it was partly your fault too!

120
00:07:54,078 --> 00:07:55,913
MS. SUZUKA OUKA

121
00:07:55,997 --> 00:07:57,206
Sorry for dropping in.

122
00:07:57,790 --> 00:07:59,834
My name is Aso.

123
00:08:02,587 --> 00:08:06,257
You're the lawyer Mr. Uramawashi
told me about, right?

124
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:07,300
What?

125
00:08:08,050 --> 00:08:11,095
He said you would consult with me
about the house.

126
00:08:11,762 --> 00:08:14,473
That man…

127
00:08:16,392 --> 00:08:19,937
There's something in that house.

128
00:08:20,771 --> 00:08:21,689
What?

129
00:08:23,524 --> 00:08:28,112
I keep hearing people's voices.

130
00:08:30,489 --> 00:08:31,490
And…

131
00:08:32,658 --> 00:08:36,412
there's this ominous presence
that makes rattling noises.

132
00:08:38,623 --> 00:08:42,251
Maybe that article was right,
and my house is a pathway for spirits!

133
00:08:42,335 --> 00:08:43,210
Ms. Ouka.

134
00:08:43,294 --> 00:08:45,463
That's it. The floor plan…

135
00:08:46,047 --> 00:08:49,592
I have to do something
about the floor plan. The floor plan!

136
00:08:49,675 --> 00:08:52,261
I have to change it.
They're telling me to change it.

137
00:08:52,345 --> 00:08:55,222
I have to change it…

138
00:08:55,306 --> 00:08:57,642
Ms. Ouka, please calm down.

139
00:08:58,559 --> 00:08:59,727
Ms. Ouka.

140
00:09:00,811 --> 00:09:02,104
Ms. Ouka.

141
00:09:03,564 --> 00:09:07,818
Would you mind
if I looked into things a little bit?

142
00:09:10,321 --> 00:09:14,450
I obtained a Power of Attorney
from Suzuka Ouka, like you told me to.

143
00:09:14,533 --> 00:09:16,327
It seems she has schizophrenia.

144
00:09:16,911 --> 00:09:19,997
When symptoms worsen,
her hallucinations become stronger,

145
00:09:20,081 --> 00:09:24,001
thoughts become disorganized,
and conversations become incoherent.

146
00:09:24,085 --> 00:09:28,756
When she was talking to me,
she started talking nonsense,

147
00:09:28,839 --> 00:09:30,925
and she was quite distraught…

148
00:09:32,009 --> 00:09:34,261
Hey, are you listening?

149
00:09:34,345 --> 00:09:36,722
I don't care about the diagnosis.

150
00:09:37,348 --> 00:09:38,599
What about the house?

151
00:09:40,685 --> 00:09:41,936
If you're so curious,

152
00:09:42,019 --> 00:09:46,065
why don't you go to Ms. Ouka's house
and check for yourself?

153
00:09:47,316 --> 00:09:50,861
That's your job, isn't it?

154
00:09:51,904 --> 00:09:52,863
Hey…

155
00:09:52,947 --> 00:09:56,617
You're the one who forced it on me!

156
00:10:10,881 --> 00:10:13,217
Excuse me.

157
00:10:18,347 --> 00:10:20,975
No one is around.

158
00:10:45,499 --> 00:10:46,584
What is this?

159
00:11:05,186 --> 00:11:06,604
What?

160
00:11:21,869 --> 00:11:23,787
Whoa! What?

161
00:11:26,832 --> 00:11:28,542
What is going on?

162
00:11:39,512 --> 00:11:40,846
SUNRAY RENOVATION

163
00:11:53,108 --> 00:11:54,276
WEEKLY TIMES

164
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:56,445
I'm Sunaga, the editor-in-chief.

165
00:11:56,529 --> 00:12:00,866
I'm Ms. Suzuka Ouka's
representing lawyer, Aso.

166
00:12:05,162 --> 00:12:07,289
Not sure what you want from us.

167
00:12:08,499 --> 00:12:09,667
Our magazine

168
00:12:10,209 --> 00:12:13,837
just publishes what the fortune teller,
Ms. Hoshimiya, says.

169
00:12:14,463 --> 00:12:18,592
Because of her fortune-telling,
Ms. Ouka's symptoms have worsened.

170
00:12:18,676 --> 00:12:20,719
Don't you feel responsible?

171
00:12:20,803 --> 00:12:24,098
It's not like we personally slandered her.

172
00:12:24,181 --> 00:12:27,351
People tend to blame us tabloids
for everything. It's a pain.

173
00:12:27,434 --> 00:12:28,269
Even so…

174
00:12:28,352 --> 00:12:29,895
Like I said earlier,

175
00:12:32,606 --> 00:12:34,650
is there any legal issue here?

176
00:12:36,193 --> 00:12:39,780
Publishing a photo of the house's exterior
isn't illegal in itself.

177
00:12:39,863 --> 00:12:42,950
But if you look closely,
laundry is visible in the shot,

178
00:12:43,033 --> 00:12:45,369
making it clear
that a woman lives there alone.

179
00:12:45,452 --> 00:12:47,913
And a part of the nameplate
is slightly visible.

180
00:12:47,997 --> 00:12:51,834
This is an infringement of privacy
and can be subject to a damages claim.

181
00:12:54,712 --> 00:12:55,796
Come in.

182
00:12:55,879 --> 00:12:58,924
Excuse me.
Editor-in-chief, you have a guest.

183
00:12:59,008 --> 00:13:00,676
Got it. I'll be right there.

184
00:13:03,679 --> 00:13:05,264
You heard her.

185
00:13:06,015 --> 00:13:07,516
Let's wrap this up.

186
00:13:11,645 --> 00:13:14,023
What a bad attitude.

187
00:13:33,626 --> 00:13:37,087
The price per square meter here
is good. The land must be worth millions.

188
00:13:37,171 --> 00:13:41,175
I heard that woman, Suzuka Ouka,
lost her husband a few years ago.

189
00:13:41,258 --> 00:13:43,385
A young widow, huh?

190
00:13:43,469 --> 00:13:46,555
And it seems her late husband
was extremely wealthy.

191
00:13:46,639 --> 00:13:48,891
She must have inherited a big fortune.

192
00:13:48,974 --> 00:13:51,352
Sounds fishy. Was she in it for the money?

193
00:13:51,435 --> 00:13:54,229
No, they were known by neighbors
as a loving couple.

194
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:56,774
The opposite of you, Mr. Kureta.

195
00:13:56,857 --> 00:13:58,025
Shut up.

196
00:13:58,734 --> 00:14:01,654
Still, her house has treasure
that attracts scammers.

197
00:14:01,737 --> 00:14:04,114
The problem is how they were targeting it.

198
00:14:04,198 --> 00:14:08,494
If you do something reckless again
and break the law, I'll report you!

199
00:14:12,539 --> 00:14:14,041
I'll have one.

200
00:14:17,628 --> 00:14:20,381
That house definitely felt strange.

201
00:14:21,173 --> 00:14:24,551
It had an eerie atmosphere.
My ears were ringing too.

202
00:14:25,219 --> 00:14:29,431
"A demon-haunted house"?

203
00:14:30,057 --> 00:14:32,977
How ridiculous. Demons don't exist.

204
00:14:37,564 --> 00:14:40,859
You don't believe in the occult?

205
00:14:42,528 --> 00:14:43,529
What?

206
00:14:44,029 --> 00:14:48,033
No way I believe it!
That stuff is for kids.

207
00:14:50,828 --> 00:14:55,249
Though,
there is one thing that bothers me.

208
00:15:00,170 --> 00:15:03,215
Sunray Renovation, huh?

209
00:15:03,298 --> 00:15:04,967
Since it's quite an old house,

210
00:15:05,050 --> 00:15:08,762
it wouldn't be strange if she were
considering rebuilding or renewing.

211
00:15:09,304 --> 00:15:11,306
SUNRAY RENOVATION

212
00:15:11,390 --> 00:15:12,266
Go ahead.

213
00:15:12,349 --> 00:15:13,475
Thank you.

214
00:15:14,351 --> 00:15:15,769
Thank you very much.

215
00:15:16,770 --> 00:15:19,106
Sorry to keep you waiting, I'm Ikuta.

216
00:15:19,189 --> 00:15:21,025
-Thank you--
-Thanks for the other day.

217
00:15:21,108 --> 00:15:24,445
We rushed here to ask you
about the kitchen renovation.

218
00:15:25,487 --> 00:15:26,655
Well…

219
00:15:26,739 --> 00:15:31,869
You know, in the showroom in Shinjuku,
we talked about doing our kitchen!

220
00:15:31,952 --> 00:15:35,122
I want to treat my dearest darling
to the finest cooking.

221
00:15:35,205 --> 00:15:37,541
Don't you remember my presentation?

222
00:15:38,292 --> 00:15:42,087
Gosh, I love you so much!

223
00:15:42,171 --> 00:15:45,257
Our love is priceless, you know!

224
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:47,926
Stop it, how embarrassing!

225
00:15:48,010 --> 00:15:50,054
I remember! Come in.

226
00:15:50,137 --> 00:15:51,847
Thank you so much.

227
00:15:52,473 --> 00:15:55,976
Ai! You went way off script!

228
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:59,146
Making it look real is important, right?

229
00:15:59,229 --> 00:16:03,650
By any chance, did you dislike it? Well?

230
00:16:03,734 --> 00:16:07,613
-Were you embarrassed?
-I didn't dislike it at all.

231
00:16:07,696 --> 00:16:11,575
It's not that I disliked it,
but I'm a man too, you know.

232
00:16:11,658 --> 00:16:12,493
Ai!

233
00:16:13,202 --> 00:16:14,995
Ai!

234
00:16:16,955 --> 00:16:19,249
-Sorry.
-Walk normally.

235
00:16:19,833 --> 00:16:24,671
I looked into it, but this guy named Ikuta
doesn't seem particularly suspicious.

236
00:16:24,755 --> 00:16:27,549
Nakazaki and I were keeping
an eye on Sunaga, and--

237
00:16:27,633 --> 00:16:28,842
What?

238
00:16:30,469 --> 00:16:31,845
This guy is Ikuta!

239
00:16:31,929 --> 00:16:33,972
So Sunaga and Ikuta are acquainted?

240
00:16:34,056 --> 00:16:35,682
It seems they meet up regularly.

241
00:16:35,766 --> 00:16:38,852
Is this related
to the Spiritual Floor Plan series?

242
00:16:38,936 --> 00:16:41,647
Maybe Hoshimiya is involved too.

243
00:16:41,730 --> 00:16:44,441
Could Sunray Renovation be a front
for Yoshin no Michi?

244
00:16:44,525 --> 00:16:49,696
Once, an organization linked to a cult
was caught selling overpriced goods.

245
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:51,907
But why team up with a renovation company?

246
00:16:51,990 --> 00:16:54,743
You should look into
Sunray Renovation a bit more.

247
00:16:54,827 --> 00:16:57,162
Yeah, so Aso will--
Wait, why are you here?

248
00:16:57,246 --> 00:17:01,458
Did you tell these people
about the case again?

249
00:17:01,542 --> 00:17:04,294
The more hands on deck, the better, right?

250
00:17:04,378 --> 00:17:06,255
Please don't interfere!

251
00:17:06,338 --> 00:17:07,631
Our lips are sealed.

252
00:17:07,714 --> 00:17:09,341
-That's not the issue.
-Sorry.

253
00:17:09,424 --> 00:17:11,510
And you never even asked me if--

254
00:17:12,219 --> 00:17:14,012
Wait. Sorry.

255
00:17:16,014 --> 00:17:17,266
Hello?

256
00:17:17,850 --> 00:17:20,018
Oh, that's right.

257
00:17:20,102 --> 00:17:22,855
No, I haven't forgotten at all.

258
00:17:23,397 --> 00:17:26,608
Yes, I'll be there soon.

259
00:17:28,735 --> 00:17:30,404
Stop everything you are doing!

260
00:17:30,487 --> 00:17:33,740
If you interfere,
I'll report you to Mr. Moriki!

261
00:17:36,034 --> 00:17:39,955
That Aso lawyer is pretty persistent.

262
00:17:40,831 --> 00:17:42,457
It might be better to pull out.

263
00:17:42,541 --> 00:17:46,170
Don't be stupid. A prime property
like that hardly ever comes around.

264
00:17:46,253 --> 00:17:48,755
If this gets out,
everything will be ruined.

265
00:17:48,839 --> 00:17:53,343
If you keep quiet, there's not
a chance in hell they'll figure it out.

266
00:17:55,345 --> 00:17:56,430
Okay.

267
00:17:56,513 --> 00:17:58,807
Then we'll continue as planned.

268
00:18:00,058 --> 00:18:02,686
I'm counting on you, Mr. Sunaga.

269
00:18:05,647 --> 00:18:07,900
Oh, I'm sorry!

270
00:18:08,901 --> 00:18:10,694
Nakazaki messed up.

271
00:18:10,777 --> 00:18:12,362
Bring the vacuum cleaner.

272
00:18:12,446 --> 00:18:13,780
I'll go get it!

273
00:18:13,864 --> 00:18:15,699
-No need.
-Move it!

274
00:18:15,782 --> 00:18:18,160
I'll clean it up, move.

275
00:18:18,243 --> 00:18:21,622
I'm just being a good mentor.

276
00:18:21,705 --> 00:18:23,457
Oh, we're sorry for the noise.

277
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:25,209
Our Nakazaki is so clumsy.

278
00:18:25,292 --> 00:18:27,085
I'm so sorry!

279
00:18:27,169 --> 00:18:29,379
Ready, set, sorry!

280
00:18:29,463 --> 00:18:30,631
What?

281
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:44,394
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

282
00:18:44,478 --> 00:18:46,980
I haven't been waiting long. It's fine.

283
00:18:47,731 --> 00:18:50,484
What a lovely restaurant! Thank you.

284
00:18:50,567 --> 00:18:52,819
We finally fulfilled our promise.

285
00:18:55,989 --> 00:18:58,992
Donghyuk, do you believe in ghosts?

286
00:18:59,076 --> 00:19:00,327
Ghosts?

287
00:19:00,410 --> 00:19:03,121
Like, being told
"a ghost is following you around,"

288
00:19:03,205 --> 00:19:04,790
then paying money for an exorcism.

289
00:19:04,873 --> 00:19:07,417
No, it doesn't really register with me.

290
00:19:08,085 --> 00:19:10,295
Right?

291
00:19:13,298 --> 00:19:14,549
A spiritual scam?

292
00:19:15,884 --> 00:19:18,178
Are you investigating a case like that?

293
00:19:18,262 --> 00:19:19,221
No.

294
00:19:20,222 --> 00:19:22,474
Korea also had such scams in the past.

295
00:19:22,557 --> 00:19:25,477
No, it's nothing like that.
It's really not.

296
00:19:26,937 --> 00:19:29,648
It's cute how terrible you are at lying.

297
00:19:30,357 --> 00:19:31,817
How did you know?

298
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:33,443
So I was right.

299
00:19:39,533 --> 00:19:42,577
Are you going undercover
to investigate a spiritual scam?

300
00:19:43,078 --> 00:19:45,956
I don't know the full picture yet,

301
00:19:46,039 --> 00:19:48,458
but that person
is strangely obsessed with it.

302
00:19:48,542 --> 00:19:51,837
-You mean Mr. Uramawashi?
-Yes. I wonder why.

303
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:53,672
Maybe because it's part of the job?

304
00:19:53,755 --> 00:19:56,758
No. He just saw it in a magazine article.

305
00:19:58,468 --> 00:20:01,305
Why did he read that tabloid anyway?

306
00:20:01,888 --> 00:20:04,808
You're investigating
that weekly magazine, right?

307
00:20:05,642 --> 00:20:08,437
Oh, no, it's nothing.

308
00:20:10,314 --> 00:20:11,606
Excuse me.

309
00:20:13,233 --> 00:20:15,277
MR. URAMAWASHI
DROP BY MY OFFICE ON THE WAY BACK

310
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:16,987
What?

311
00:20:26,288 --> 00:20:28,957
Mr. Uramawashi!

312
00:20:37,424 --> 00:20:39,009
Mr. Uramawashi!

313
00:20:40,594 --> 00:20:43,680
Are you here, Mr. Uramawashi?

314
00:20:45,265 --> 00:20:48,518
He asked me to come, and then went out…

315
00:20:51,938 --> 00:20:53,148
Again!

316
00:20:58,570 --> 00:20:59,988
This…

317
00:21:04,159 --> 00:21:07,579
I'm sorry!

318
00:21:07,662 --> 00:21:08,747
I'm sorry…

319
00:21:09,581 --> 00:21:10,582
Mr. Uramawashi?

320
00:21:12,125 --> 00:21:13,668
I thought…

321
00:21:14,336 --> 00:21:15,837
You thought what?

322
00:21:16,505 --> 00:21:18,715
You thought this place was haunted, right?

323
00:21:20,175 --> 00:21:23,387
There's no way.

324
00:21:23,470 --> 00:21:26,515
I'm just tired,
thanks to a certain someone.

325
00:21:28,433 --> 00:21:30,143
I see.

326
00:21:31,436 --> 00:21:32,938
What is it?

327
00:21:33,647 --> 00:21:35,524
It's late already. Go home.

328
00:21:37,275 --> 00:21:38,610
What?

329
00:21:42,572 --> 00:21:45,158
But I came all the way here…

330
00:21:45,242 --> 00:21:48,537
I ended things early to come here, why…

331
00:21:48,620 --> 00:21:51,790
Why must he always treat me this way?

332
00:22:23,363 --> 00:22:24,781
Calling it "demon-haunted"…

333
00:22:24,865 --> 00:22:29,369
-The landlady went hysterical?
-That house definitely felt strange.

334
00:23:05,071 --> 00:23:07,407
God is in the details.

335
00:23:08,241 --> 00:23:11,494
The devil hides in the cracks.

336
00:23:14,122 --> 00:23:17,000
The acquisition of the Hoshino Apartment
is complete.

337
00:23:17,584 --> 00:23:21,087
That was faster than expected.
Impressive work.

338
00:23:21,171 --> 00:23:23,590
I'm glad I could be of service.

339
00:23:23,673 --> 00:23:27,510
They probably didn't expect things
to turn out like this either.

340
00:23:28,470 --> 00:23:31,264
Still, you've really grown
into someone reliable.

341
00:23:32,307 --> 00:23:34,976
I wish Mr. Nitou could see this.

342
00:23:35,060 --> 00:23:38,271
I will finish the job thoroughly,
for my father's sake.

343
00:23:42,192 --> 00:23:43,944
He really pisses me off!

344
00:23:44,027 --> 00:23:47,405
But the problem's with you too.
Why are you so scared?

345
00:23:47,489 --> 00:23:49,407
I don't really know,

346
00:23:49,491 --> 00:23:52,452
my ears suddenly started ringing,
and I got dizzy.

347
00:23:53,912 --> 00:23:55,956
So a demon lives there?

348
00:23:56,039 --> 00:23:58,250
That man certainly is a demon.

349
00:23:58,333 --> 00:24:00,669
And what is that demon's motive?

350
00:24:00,752 --> 00:24:02,379
I want to ask that too!

351
00:24:02,462 --> 00:24:06,633
Was it the content of the article
that caught his attention, or…

352
00:24:06,716 --> 00:24:09,177
No one understands
how an eccentric thinks.

353
00:24:09,261 --> 00:24:11,429
Honestly, I don't even want to understand.

354
00:24:11,513 --> 00:24:15,308
Even so, it's a ridiculous series,
isn't it?

355
00:24:15,392 --> 00:24:19,521
Just snooping around
other people's houses, writing nonsense.

356
00:24:19,604 --> 00:24:22,482
This Sunaga guy is the absolute worst.

357
00:24:24,943 --> 00:24:26,194
Oh!

358
00:24:26,278 --> 00:24:28,363
I looked into
Sunray Renovation's reputation.

359
00:24:28,446 --> 00:24:31,866
They repeatedly went door-to-door
offering free house inspections,

360
00:24:31,950 --> 00:24:35,287
then claimed bad feng shui
or issues with energy flow

361
00:24:35,370 --> 00:24:37,539
to push expensive renovations.

362
00:24:37,622 --> 00:24:40,542
I found out who manages
their sales. It's all Ikuta!

363
00:24:40,625 --> 00:24:42,711
That guy really is up to no good!

364
00:24:42,794 --> 00:24:45,505
Perhaps their boss
is that cult leader Hoshimiya?

365
00:24:45,588 --> 00:24:49,843
If we can establish the connection,
we can wrap this up all at once, but…

366
00:24:49,926 --> 00:24:53,680
Do people actually fall for those
sales pitches? Feng shui and all that.

367
00:24:53,763 --> 00:24:54,889
I might believe it.

368
00:24:54,973 --> 00:24:56,599
Nakazaki, you're spiritual, huh?

369
00:24:56,683 --> 00:24:57,851
I really am!

370
00:24:57,934 --> 00:24:59,894
Maybe one in a hundred believes it?

371
00:24:59,978 --> 00:25:01,354
That's way too inefficient.

372
00:25:01,438 --> 00:25:05,066
And if that household doesn't have money,
it's meaningless anyway.

373
00:25:05,775 --> 00:25:09,029
DEMON-HAUNTED HOUSE?

374
00:25:11,448 --> 00:25:13,033
All right.

375
00:25:13,825 --> 00:25:15,118
This should be all.

376
00:25:15,201 --> 00:25:16,703
Thank you very much.

377
00:25:29,424 --> 00:25:30,258
Found one.

378
00:25:30,342 --> 00:25:31,343
Me too.

379
00:25:35,930 --> 00:25:37,057
THE TRUE FACE OF…

380
00:25:37,140 --> 00:25:38,266
I knew it.

381
00:25:38,350 --> 00:25:39,476
WEEKLY TIMES

382
00:25:39,559 --> 00:25:40,977
Here.

383
00:25:44,773 --> 00:25:47,359
EDITORIAL DEPARTMENT
RYUTARO SUNAGA

384
00:25:54,866 --> 00:25:56,076
Good work today!

385
00:25:56,159 --> 00:25:57,577
Out of my way!

386
00:26:00,246 --> 00:26:01,456
Do you have a moment?

387
00:26:01,539 --> 00:26:03,875
What's wrong? Your voice sounds scary.

388
00:26:04,793 --> 00:26:05,668
This.

389
00:26:06,294 --> 00:26:07,670
Please explain it.

390
00:26:08,213 --> 00:26:10,006
"Crooked lawyer."

391
00:26:10,924 --> 00:26:14,761
Ten years ago, when Mrs. Shiramoto
was arrested on suspicion of murder,

392
00:26:14,844 --> 00:26:17,847
there was a journalist
who persistently criticized her.

393
00:26:17,931 --> 00:26:20,100
That was Ryutaro Sunaga.

394
00:26:20,183 --> 00:26:21,643
Because of the articles,

395
00:26:21,726 --> 00:26:24,854
public opinion swung heavily
toward bashing Mrs. Shiramoto.

396
00:26:24,938 --> 00:26:28,733
And after a trial
that was mostly just for show,

397
00:26:28,817 --> 00:26:30,860
before anyone knew it, she was convicted.

398
00:26:31,820 --> 00:26:36,116
Isn't Sunaga the real target of this case?

399
00:26:37,283 --> 00:26:40,787
I've had enough of being jerked around
and kept in the dark.

400
00:26:40,870 --> 00:26:42,122
Please tell me.

401
00:26:42,205 --> 00:26:45,625
Why are you investigating the case
of Miyuki Shiramoto?

402
00:26:45,708 --> 00:26:47,669
What relationship do you have with her?

403
00:26:47,752 --> 00:26:51,089
What's going on?
You're being awfully loud.

404
00:26:51,673 --> 00:26:52,924
This…

405
00:26:53,508 --> 00:26:55,677
Please explain this to me.

406
00:26:55,760 --> 00:26:56,678
CORDIA LAWYER

407
00:26:58,513 --> 00:27:01,015
Miyuki Shiramoto.

408
00:27:03,435 --> 00:27:05,061
Miyuki is my younger sister.

409
00:27:06,771 --> 00:27:09,023
Why didn't you tell me?

410
00:27:10,608 --> 00:27:12,777
-Did she ask?
-No.

411
00:27:13,486 --> 00:27:17,574
-You must be lying. You must be.
-But you saw her maiden name.

412
00:27:17,657 --> 00:27:20,243
No, but that's impossible.
I don't want to believe it.

413
00:27:20,326 --> 00:27:22,662
Mr. Uramawashi
and Mrs. Shiramoto are related?

414
00:27:22,745 --> 00:27:24,831
No, I physically can't accept it!

415
00:27:24,914 --> 00:27:27,041
What? No…

416
00:27:27,834 --> 00:27:29,294
Aso.

417
00:27:30,462 --> 00:27:32,839
A lawyer is someone

418
00:27:33,715 --> 00:27:36,885
who separates emotions from facts.

419
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:42,765
What do you plan to do
after investigating Sunaga?

420
00:27:43,892 --> 00:27:46,394
You'll figure that out eventually.

421
00:27:48,354 --> 00:27:49,981
Now, back to work.

422
00:27:50,064 --> 00:27:51,566
That's right, work.

423
00:27:51,649 --> 00:27:54,319
Aso is so scary.

424
00:27:55,236 --> 00:27:56,446
A lie!

425
00:27:56,529 --> 00:28:00,492
It must be a lie. I can't believe it.
They don't look alike at all.

426
00:28:00,575 --> 00:28:02,869
Calm down, have another glass.

427
00:28:02,952 --> 00:28:04,496
Here, have some salad.

428
00:28:04,579 --> 00:28:05,788
They don't look alike.

429
00:28:05,872 --> 00:28:07,248
Not at all.

430
00:28:07,332 --> 00:28:09,334
I was the only one who knew.

431
00:28:09,417 --> 00:28:10,835
Why didn't you tell us?

432
00:28:10,919 --> 00:28:12,837
Wait, you all didn't know?

433
00:28:12,921 --> 00:28:15,006
-No.
-First time hearing it.

434
00:28:15,089 --> 00:28:18,801
Well, it's not my place to say.

435
00:28:18,885 --> 00:28:22,514
More importantly, Ms. Aso,
how did you know Mrs. Shiramoto?

436
00:28:23,515 --> 00:28:26,809
I've been a troublesome kid
since I was little.

437
00:28:26,893 --> 00:28:28,811
I didn't have many friends.

438
00:28:31,856 --> 00:28:32,815
What?

439
00:28:32,899 --> 00:28:34,692
You won't contradict me?

440
00:28:35,443 --> 00:28:37,695
No, you aren't difficult at all!

441
00:28:37,779 --> 00:28:39,823
I never thought so! Really!

442
00:28:39,906 --> 00:28:40,824
It's fine.

443
00:28:40,907 --> 00:28:43,076
Stop. Thank you.

444
00:28:44,661 --> 00:28:45,870
What happened next?

445
00:28:47,330 --> 00:28:52,252
Then, during a middle school social
studies field trip, I met Mrs. Shiramoto,

446
00:28:52,335 --> 00:28:54,337
and they let us spectate a trial.

447
00:28:55,004 --> 00:28:59,008
Seeing Mrs. Shiramoto
fight relentlessly for her client

448
00:28:59,092 --> 00:29:00,385
moved me.

449
00:29:01,177 --> 00:29:04,055
Why did you give a statement
that differed from the facts?

450
00:29:05,098 --> 00:29:07,809
No matter what I said,
nobody would believe me.

451
00:29:08,726 --> 00:29:10,770
I just wanted to get it over with.

452
00:29:11,479 --> 00:29:12,689
Even so,

453
00:29:13,231 --> 00:29:18,194
there is no need to admit to things that
aren't true and lie in court, you know.

454
00:29:24,617 --> 00:29:25,660
Excuse me.

455
00:29:27,537 --> 00:29:28,580
Ms. Aso?

456
00:29:29,330 --> 00:29:30,790
You came to watch me?

457
00:29:34,210 --> 00:29:35,712
You were really cool.

458
00:29:36,838 --> 00:29:39,465
Thank you. I'm happy to hear that.

459
00:29:42,594 --> 00:29:43,678
I…

460
00:29:45,930 --> 00:29:49,058
I hate lies,

461
00:29:52,061 --> 00:29:54,480
and I can never tolerate unfairness,

462
00:29:56,816 --> 00:29:57,942
so…

463
00:29:59,444 --> 00:30:02,196
I always get into fights with everyone.

464
00:30:09,537 --> 00:30:11,456
You've done nothing wrong.

465
00:30:12,498 --> 00:30:14,584
Stay just as you are.

466
00:30:15,835 --> 00:30:19,672
However,
there are many different kinds of lies.

467
00:30:20,340 --> 00:30:22,759
Instead of condemning lies as a whole,

468
00:30:23,384 --> 00:30:28,640
try thinking about the true intention
and meaning behind why a person lied.

469
00:30:34,062 --> 00:30:37,106
I see, so that's what happened.

470
00:30:37,190 --> 00:30:38,191
Yes.

471
00:30:39,275 --> 00:30:43,279
So, what is Mr. Uramawashi trying to do?

472
00:30:44,072 --> 00:30:45,448
About that…

473
00:30:46,783 --> 00:30:49,160
I guess we will find out as we go along.

474
00:30:49,786 --> 00:30:51,204
What do you mean?

475
00:30:52,163 --> 00:30:57,085
Everyone has their own reasons,
but we can't leave those siblings alone.

476
00:31:01,673 --> 00:31:03,967
I see.

477
00:31:04,634 --> 00:31:07,261
Then, I'll turn a blind eye this time.

478
00:31:07,345 --> 00:31:10,223
But no breaking the law, okay?

479
00:31:10,932 --> 00:31:12,266
Of course not.

480
00:31:12,350 --> 00:31:13,559
That's a given.

481
00:31:13,643 --> 00:31:17,230
What kind of history do you all have
with the Uramawashi siblings?

482
00:31:17,313 --> 00:31:19,399
Well, you know…

483
00:31:19,482 --> 00:31:20,566
That's private.

484
00:31:20,650 --> 00:31:22,902
What? But I just told you mine.

485
00:31:22,986 --> 00:31:25,488
Calm down, let's eat while it's hot.

486
00:31:25,571 --> 00:31:27,949
I just told you mine, didn't I?

487
00:31:31,536 --> 00:31:32,954
-Staying overnight?
-Yes.

488
00:31:33,037 --> 00:31:36,833
Ms. Ouka is being discharged.
She said she's anxious about being alone.

489
00:31:36,916 --> 00:31:40,628
I'll stay there one night,
and if nothing happens, she'll feel safe.

490
00:31:40,712 --> 00:31:43,840
But you know, sometimes things happen.

491
00:31:43,923 --> 00:31:45,341
Why don't I go with you--

492
00:31:45,425 --> 00:31:48,261
No, having you there
just increases the danger.

493
00:31:48,344 --> 00:31:49,887
-What?
-I'll go.

494
00:31:49,971 --> 00:31:51,514
No, please let me go.

495
00:31:51,597 --> 00:31:53,725
Let me go. It's safer.

496
00:31:53,808 --> 00:31:55,810
No, Saba, you're useless.

497
00:31:55,893 --> 00:31:57,937
You would make it more dangerous!

498
00:31:58,021 --> 00:31:59,647
-What do you mean?
-I said I'll go!

499
00:31:59,731 --> 00:32:01,607
-No, you're useless.
-And you are--

500
00:32:01,691 --> 00:32:03,443
-It's better if I go.
-That would be pointless!

501
00:32:03,526 --> 00:32:06,946
Then, let's just have Ms. Aso decide.

502
00:32:07,030 --> 00:32:08,364
That's fine by me.

503
00:32:09,323 --> 00:32:10,700
Which of us do you prefer?

504
00:32:15,121 --> 00:32:17,457
Jeez, why me?

505
00:32:17,540 --> 00:32:21,002
Because everyone else is so unreliable.

506
00:32:23,379 --> 00:32:24,964
Ms. Aso!

507
00:32:25,048 --> 00:32:26,549
Thank you so much for coming.

508
00:32:26,632 --> 00:32:30,219
It's nothing. We're here with you,
so you can feel at ease.

509
00:32:30,303 --> 00:32:31,804
Here, just in case.

510
00:32:31,888 --> 00:32:32,972
SALT

511
00:32:33,056 --> 00:32:36,100
It's okay, you don't need to be so scared.

512
00:32:36,184 --> 00:32:37,685
Follow me.

513
00:32:41,105 --> 00:32:42,648
Excuse us.

514
00:32:43,274 --> 00:32:46,486
At least go to the bathroom by yourself.

515
00:32:46,569 --> 00:32:48,613
It's not super terrifying but…

516
00:32:48,696 --> 00:32:50,740
You're not a child, you know.

517
00:32:50,823 --> 00:32:52,200
Just in case…

518
00:32:53,743 --> 00:32:56,788
Hey, that's your own face.

519
00:32:56,871 --> 00:32:57,955
Ms. Aso.

520
00:32:59,791 --> 00:33:02,210
The futons are ready.

521
00:33:02,293 --> 00:33:03,920
Thank you very much.

522
00:33:06,631 --> 00:33:08,800
You were scared too, right?

523
00:33:08,883 --> 00:33:10,593
I wasn't.

524
00:33:12,095 --> 00:33:16,140
The series is doing well,
and there's a special issue coming up.

525
00:33:16,224 --> 00:33:17,975
That's great news.

526
00:33:18,059 --> 00:33:20,394
I'm also thinking about a new project.

527
00:33:20,478 --> 00:33:23,856
We go undercover to investigate houses
with a bad floor plan.

528
00:33:23,940 --> 00:33:26,484
It might be better
not to make it too comical.

529
00:33:26,567 --> 00:33:29,612
No, if we do it, we have to go all out.

530
00:33:30,530 --> 00:33:34,992
Even in this day and age,
an approach like this still catches on.

531
00:33:35,076 --> 00:33:36,911
In any era,

532
00:33:36,994 --> 00:33:40,498
people are drawn to things
that make no sense.

533
00:33:40,581 --> 00:33:41,916
Exactly as you say.

534
00:33:42,500 --> 00:33:46,587
Still, I couldn't believe ghosts
and all that stuff would be a hit.

535
00:33:48,005 --> 00:33:49,674
Do you not believe in it?

536
00:33:49,757 --> 00:33:52,218
Of course I do.

537
00:33:53,219 --> 00:33:55,096
Ms. Hoshimiya, go ahead.

538
00:33:55,179 --> 00:33:58,808
If you make light of it,
you'll end up regretting it.

539
00:33:59,475 --> 00:34:00,351
Excuse me?

540
00:34:00,935 --> 00:34:03,354
It's a dog-eat-dog world.

541
00:34:03,980 --> 00:34:07,650
I won't fault you for taking advantage
of people's weaknesses.

542
00:34:08,276 --> 00:34:09,443
However,

543
00:34:10,945 --> 00:34:13,781
the fact that you're targeting someone

544
00:34:14,532 --> 00:34:18,244
means someone else is targeting you too.

545
00:34:21,122 --> 00:34:23,082
-This way, please.
-Yes.

546
00:34:23,166 --> 00:34:24,375
Say cheese.

547
00:34:26,002 --> 00:34:27,295
One more.

548
00:34:28,629 --> 00:34:30,506
And another…

549
00:34:44,645 --> 00:34:45,646
Maki.

550
00:34:46,147 --> 00:34:47,356
Maki?

551
00:34:52,904 --> 00:34:54,113
This is…

552
00:34:54,614 --> 00:34:56,490
This is what happened in the office.

553
00:34:59,911 --> 00:35:03,372
It's all in my head.

554
00:35:03,456 --> 00:35:06,500
It's all in my head.

555
00:35:06,584 --> 00:35:07,627
It's not!

556
00:35:08,961 --> 00:35:10,004
Is something wrong?

557
00:35:10,087 --> 00:35:11,380
Hey…

558
00:35:12,632 --> 00:35:14,091
Hey…

559
00:35:17,678 --> 00:35:19,388
Ms. Ouka!

560
00:35:19,472 --> 00:35:21,641
What? Stop it already!

561
00:35:22,475 --> 00:35:23,726
-Stop it!
-It's okay.

562
00:35:23,809 --> 00:35:25,394
I'm right here with you.

563
00:35:27,396 --> 00:35:28,564
Help me!

564
00:35:32,944 --> 00:35:33,903
What?

565
00:35:34,737 --> 00:35:37,031
Who is it?

566
00:35:38,324 --> 00:35:39,700
Who's there?

567
00:35:45,248 --> 00:35:46,165
Are you okay?

568
00:35:47,750 --> 00:35:48,709
A thief!

569
00:35:48,793 --> 00:35:51,254
-Call the police!
-Wait, shut up a little.

570
00:35:51,337 --> 00:35:53,047
Habu? What are you doing?

571
00:35:53,130 --> 00:35:54,590
I heard you scream.

572
00:35:54,674 --> 00:35:55,800
You were peeping?

573
00:35:55,883 --> 00:35:59,136
No, that's not it.
Mr. Uramawashi told me to.

574
00:35:59,220 --> 00:36:00,346
-Look.
-What?

575
00:36:09,146 --> 00:36:12,108
Man, that was so easy.

576
00:36:12,191 --> 00:36:15,319
That Ikuta guy fell for it so easily.

577
00:36:15,403 --> 00:36:17,446
Hey, is what you said earlier true?

578
00:36:17,530 --> 00:36:18,739
Yeah.

579
00:36:18,823 --> 00:36:22,285
Evidence was found,
so the Ouka house issue is resolved.

580
00:36:22,868 --> 00:36:24,287
Ms. Aso said so.

581
00:36:24,370 --> 00:36:26,914
Then how long do we have
to keep up the surveillance?

582
00:36:26,998 --> 00:36:28,749
She said we can stop by tomorrow.

583
00:36:28,833 --> 00:36:30,251
Lucky.

584
00:36:30,334 --> 00:36:34,380
WEEKLY TIMES

585
00:36:38,009 --> 00:36:38,843
Yes?

586
00:36:39,844 --> 00:36:41,804
Things have turned bad.

587
00:36:41,887 --> 00:36:43,764
Mr. Ikuta? What happened?

588
00:36:43,848 --> 00:36:44,932
They found out.

589
00:36:45,016 --> 00:36:45,850
Huh?

590
00:36:45,933 --> 00:36:47,977
Come to the Ouka house immediately.

591
00:36:51,188 --> 00:36:52,481
Mr. Ikuta?

592
00:36:58,154 --> 00:36:59,947
Hey!

593
00:37:00,656 --> 00:37:01,532
Hey!

594
00:37:03,576 --> 00:37:06,162
Hey, where did you go?

595
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:13,502
This, huh? How creepy.

596
00:37:15,046 --> 00:37:16,172
Whoa.

597
00:37:18,215 --> 00:37:19,216
Hey!

598
00:37:23,095 --> 00:37:24,638
What are you doing?

599
00:37:28,434 --> 00:37:29,685
What is going on?

600
00:37:29,769 --> 00:37:33,606
The way the wind blows,
the tilt of the roof.

601
00:37:34,607 --> 00:37:38,694
People mistake a subtle sense
of discomfort for fear.

602
00:37:39,737 --> 00:37:45,242
What was used this time
was infrasound around 19 Hz.

603
00:37:46,035 --> 00:37:48,871
Even though people can't hear it,
in some people,

604
00:37:48,954 --> 00:37:51,207
it creates a feeling
of pressure or anxiety.

605
00:37:51,999 --> 00:37:53,501
What is he talking about?

606
00:37:54,960 --> 00:37:57,713
The top of the old well
in the garden was sealed,

607
00:37:57,797 --> 00:38:00,132
with pipes connecting
the sewer pipe to the well

608
00:38:00,216 --> 00:38:03,302
and connecting the well
to under the floorboards.

609
00:38:03,386 --> 00:38:05,930
Every time wind passes through
from underground,

610
00:38:06,013 --> 00:38:09,183
the vibrations are amplified.
It was designed that way.

611
00:38:09,850 --> 00:38:11,811
Helmholtz resonance.

612
00:38:13,104 --> 00:38:16,440
The same principle as blowing
across the mouth of a bottle.

613
00:38:18,734 --> 00:38:20,820
The air inside the well

614
00:38:21,612 --> 00:38:23,030
resonated.

615
00:38:23,989 --> 00:38:25,449
That voice too?

616
00:38:26,450 --> 00:38:31,038
The low resonant sounds and wind noise
could be mistaken for a human voice, too.

617
00:38:31,580 --> 00:38:33,791
Then, what about the house shaking?

618
00:38:37,670 --> 00:38:41,924
The pressure fluctuations
intensified by the well's resonance

619
00:38:43,092 --> 00:38:47,304
were transmitted to the house
through the air and pipes under the floor.

620
00:38:50,099 --> 00:38:51,183
Causing it to resonate.

621
00:38:51,267 --> 00:38:53,102
Resonance?

622
00:38:53,811 --> 00:38:56,355
The floorboards and furniture are loose,

623
00:38:56,439 --> 00:39:00,693
so with resonance,
they rattled all at once.

624
00:39:00,776 --> 00:39:01,902
In short,

625
00:39:02,486 --> 00:39:08,200
somebody intentionally
created an environment

626
00:39:09,702 --> 00:39:11,704
where paranormal phenomena would occur.

627
00:39:11,787 --> 00:39:14,290
I don't know what you are talking about.

628
00:39:20,087 --> 00:39:21,255
Mr. Ikuta.

629
00:39:21,964 --> 00:39:25,468
When I intentionally leaked information
to him that the trick

630
00:39:25,551 --> 00:39:29,472
behind the paranormal phenomena
was solved, he fell right into the trap.

631
00:39:35,186 --> 00:39:37,813
I don't know anything.
He did everything on his own.

632
00:39:37,897 --> 00:39:39,857
Are you still going to play dumb?

633
00:39:41,525 --> 00:39:44,278
Then how do you explain this?

634
00:39:55,122 --> 00:39:58,334
NO RECORDS OF THESE MEETINGS
EVER TAKING PLACE

635
00:39:59,293 --> 00:40:01,420
HE DID SAY THIS
BUT IT WAS TAKEN FROM ANOTHER INTERVIEW

636
00:40:01,504 --> 00:40:02,588
This…

637
00:40:05,925 --> 00:40:11,472
You took money and wrote baseless,
slanderous articles in exchange.

638
00:40:12,473 --> 00:40:15,601
I looked into each of them thoroughly.

639
00:40:16,143 --> 00:40:17,144
What?

640
00:40:17,228 --> 00:40:18,687
You investigated everything?

641
00:40:18,771 --> 00:40:21,649
I will publish all of it.

642
00:40:22,399 --> 00:40:23,692
What a shame.

643
00:40:24,235 --> 00:40:26,362
Your journalist career is over now.

644
00:40:27,363 --> 00:40:32,243
He's far from just being finished.
In this day and age, imagine the backlash.

645
00:40:32,326 --> 00:40:36,580
The testimonies
and fact-checking are all complete.

646
00:40:39,166 --> 00:40:40,459
How does it feel?

647
00:40:41,418 --> 00:40:45,214
To be stripped bare
and exposed to the public?

648
00:40:46,257 --> 00:40:47,883
Forgive me.

649
00:40:49,009 --> 00:40:50,928
It was just a lapse of judgment.

650
00:40:55,808 --> 00:40:59,979
At first, I was just writing
some flattering articles for pocket money,

651
00:41:00,062 --> 00:41:02,481
but gradually it spiraled out of control.

652
00:41:05,359 --> 00:41:07,069
Answer me just one thing.

653
00:41:07,152 --> 00:41:08,153
Yes?

654
00:41:12,324 --> 00:41:14,743
The article about Mrs. Shiramoto.

655
00:41:15,536 --> 00:41:17,204
Was that fabricated too?

656
00:41:25,754 --> 00:41:28,007
Is that your answer?

657
00:41:30,551 --> 00:41:33,637
The one who ordered
the article was Furuse.

658
00:41:34,763 --> 00:41:35,889
Wasn't it?

659
00:41:36,640 --> 00:41:39,184
That's not true.
I have no idea who that is.

660
00:41:39,977 --> 00:41:43,814
Please. I have a family. Please let me go.

661
00:41:43,897 --> 00:41:46,275
We've already confirmed you're single.

662
00:41:48,319 --> 00:41:51,155
Your lies are so easily exposed.

663
00:41:53,073 --> 00:41:55,826
You only have two options.

664
00:41:56,869 --> 00:41:59,663
Either do as I say…

665
00:42:02,249 --> 00:42:04,501
or lose everything.

666
00:42:14,261 --> 00:42:18,015
This way, then like this,
and here, right here.

667
00:42:18,098 --> 00:42:19,183
Yeah.

668
00:42:19,266 --> 00:42:21,226
Shut up! Stop doing that already!

669
00:42:21,310 --> 00:42:22,269
Sorry.

670
00:42:22,353 --> 00:42:23,937
They tamper with a house,

671
00:42:24,021 --> 00:42:27,816
then do cold-call sales to push
expensive renovations.

672
00:42:27,900 --> 00:42:31,612
They bill roughly ten times
the market rate.

673
00:42:31,695 --> 00:42:34,740
Cult leader Shion Hoshimiya
didn't know anything, right?

674
00:42:35,324 --> 00:42:39,161
Her followers were using her religion
to push her spiritual scam.

675
00:42:39,244 --> 00:42:43,582
Still, it's a good thing Sunaga believed
that whole record of fabrications.

676
00:42:43,666 --> 00:42:45,626
Believed?

677
00:42:45,709 --> 00:42:47,878
We did investigate, but truth be told,

678
00:42:47,961 --> 00:42:51,382
we failed to fact-check
almost all of the articles.

679
00:42:51,465 --> 00:42:54,885
What do you mean almost all?
So you were able to fact-check some?

680
00:42:56,845 --> 00:42:58,263
Only this recent article.

681
00:42:58,347 --> 00:43:00,307
What was that talk earlier?

682
00:43:03,686 --> 00:43:04,520
It was…

683
00:43:04,603 --> 00:43:05,562
What?

684
00:43:06,188 --> 00:43:07,523
-A…
-A?

685
00:43:08,691 --> 00:43:10,442
-Bluff.
-Bluff.

686
00:43:15,781 --> 00:43:17,866
I'll deal with that later.

687
00:43:18,492 --> 00:43:22,871
More importantly, tell me about
this article you're having Sunaga write.

688
00:43:22,955 --> 00:43:24,581
"About the murder

689
00:43:24,665 --> 00:43:27,960
of Representative Furuse's secretary
ten years ago,

690
00:43:28,043 --> 00:43:30,003
despite insufficient fact-checking,

691
00:43:30,087 --> 00:43:32,381
I wrote articles
manipulating public opinion

692
00:43:32,464 --> 00:43:37,177
to make it look like
Mrs. Miyuki Shiramoto was the culprit.

693
00:43:37,761 --> 00:43:42,558
Former attorney Miyuki Shiramoto
may actually be innocent."

694
00:43:44,601 --> 00:43:48,856
Mrs. Shiramoto really is innocent?

695
00:43:49,440 --> 00:43:51,400
That's what I'm investigating now.

696
00:43:51,483 --> 00:43:54,695
If so, why don't you file for a retrial?

697
00:43:55,946 --> 00:43:58,365
She doesn't want to.

698
00:44:00,492 --> 00:44:03,162
-Excuse us.
-The police?

699
00:44:03,245 --> 00:44:05,289
Wait a moment.

700
00:44:06,623 --> 00:44:08,208
Mr. Naoto Uramawashi,

701
00:44:08,709 --> 00:44:12,504
an arrest warrant has been issued for you.

702
00:44:16,550 --> 00:44:17,551
Stand up.

703
00:44:33,776 --> 00:44:34,902
Let's go.

704
00:44:52,336 --> 00:44:53,545
Come in.

705
00:44:56,006 --> 00:44:59,885
I've put a stop to the article.
I'll also make sure Sunaga stays quiet.

706
00:44:59,968 --> 00:45:00,886
Okay.

707
00:45:00,969 --> 00:45:02,262
Excuse me.

708
00:45:30,374 --> 00:45:32,167
Wait a moment!

709
00:45:32,251 --> 00:45:34,211
-I'm a lawyer!
-Stay back.

710
00:45:34,294 --> 00:45:36,838
Which police station are you from?
I'll follow!

711
00:45:38,924 --> 00:45:40,384
Mr. Uramawashi.

712
00:45:47,057 --> 00:45:48,809
So he was an enemy, after all.

713
00:45:48,892 --> 00:45:51,144
We thought we had him cornered, but…

714
00:45:51,228 --> 00:45:53,647
I've taken care
of the architecture office.

715
00:45:53,730 --> 00:45:56,108
We may never meet again.

716
00:45:56,191 --> 00:45:58,944
A Korean man visited me
and said he would handle the rest.

717
00:45:59,027 --> 00:46:00,821
Chef Kajiwara, I was waiting for you.

718
00:46:00,904 --> 00:46:03,323
Mr. Uramawashi,
you must have a bigger endgame.

719
00:46:03,407 --> 00:46:06,618
You should be able to draw it too.
The blueprint of lies.

720
00:46:07,119 --> 00:46:08,078
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

